urname>Grzelakowska-Sztabert</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Colombatto</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Manteuffel-Cymborowska</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Agmatine modulates the in vivo biosynthesis and interconversion of polyamines and cell proliferation</article-title><source>Biochim Biophys Acta</source><year>2003</year><volume>1619</volume><fpage>159</fpage><lpage>166</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12527112</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>XC</given-names></name><name><surname>Reis</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Agmatine selectively blocks the N-methyl-D-aspartate subclass of glutamate receptor channels in rat hippocampal neurons</article-title><source>J Pharmacol Exp Ther</source><year>1999</year><volume>288</volume><fpage>544</fpage><lpage>549</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9918557</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gilad</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Salame</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Rabey</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilad</surname><given-names>VH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Agmatine treatment is neuroprotective in rodent brain injury models</article-title><source>Life Sci</source><year>1996</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>PL41</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0024-3205(95)02274-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Yenari</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Giffard</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Cho</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Agmatine reduces infarct area in a mouse model of transient focal cerebral ischemia and protects cultured neurons from ischemia-like injury</article-title><source>Exp Neurol</source><year>2004</year><volume>189</volume><fpage>122</fpage><lpage>130</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15296842</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.expneurol.2004.05.029</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>DI</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Suh</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>YJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Chung</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Protective effect of agmatine on a reperfusion model after transient cerebral ischemia: Temporal evolution on perfusion MR imaging and histopathologic findings</article-title><source>AJNR Am J Neuroradiol</source><year>2006</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>780</fpage><lpage>785</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16611764</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>MY</given-names></name><name><surname>Piletz</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Halaris</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Regunathan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of agmatine against cell death induced by NMDA and glutamate in neurons and PC12 cells</article-title><source>Cell Mol Neurobiol</source><year>2003</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>865</fpage><lpage>872</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14514037</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1023/A:1025069407173</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>WP</given-names></name><name><surname>Iyo</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Miguel-Hidalgo</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Regunathan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>MY</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Agmatine protects against cell damage induced by NMDA and glutamate in cultured hippocampal neurons</article-title><source>Brain Res</source><year>2006</year><volume>1084</volume><fpage>210</fpage><lpage>216</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16546145</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.brainres.2006.02.024</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gilad</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilad</surname><given-names>VH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Accelerated functional recovery and neuroprotection by agmatine after spinal cord ischemia in rats</article-title><source>Neurosci Lett</source><year>2000</year><volume>296</volume><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>100</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11108990</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0304-3940(00)01625-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kotil</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuscuoglu</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirali</surname><given-names>M</given-na